Z||000000||Jncomutt||11-11-2001||10:55 PM||||How do I know if I need to replace my rear calipers?  The ebrake works but I don't think they work normally.  My braking is terrible.  The car barely slows down, but if I push the pedal harder, the fronts just lock up.  Also, I think the pass. side drags some times after I put the ebrake down.  (Yes the cable is good, and the lever moves back, just that the pad does't retract)||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||11-11-2001||11:23 PM||||The cables could get stuck inside their jackets. Try to lube them if this is the case. You could also rebuild the calipers if they are sticking.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||11-11-2001||11:48 PM||||Hey, Great to hear from someone else living in CT!!!<P>Both cables are brand new, I had to replace then because the people that did my clutch f'ed em up somehow and they siezed with the brake up.  (I found out the hard way, drove home with the brake still partially on, hubs grew red hot, smoking badly, etc.)<P>I'll have to look into the Rebuild thing, I don't know much about it.  Anyone have any info to share???||||reg||1
